  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Academy for Women Entrepreneurs (AWE) - HOCO Dynamics</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HOCO Dynamics, founded by AWE award recipient Sheila Koech, seeks to provide eco-friendly alternative construction materials, allowing more people to be able to afford and have access to decent housing in Kilifi County by making use of coconut husks waste abundant in the area. By utilizing the coconut husks waste to make building blocks and panels, HOCO Dynamics will provide sustainable and affordable housing alternatives while creating jobs; 10 directly and 30 indirectly, alleviating poverty in Kilifi County. The eco-friendly building materials will help reduce carbon emission by 35%. In one year, they aim to have made and sold construction materials to build 30 new standard 2 bedroom houses using the husks.</narrative>
  </description>
